		"text": "DHL Express Announces Annual Price Adjustments in the U.S.\n\nDHL Express, the world’s leading international express services provider, announced a 5.9% general average shipment price adjustment for U.S. account holders that will take effect on January 1, 2027.\n\nDHL Supply Chain Launches New Logistics Solution for U.S. Health Systems\n\nBuilt for modern health systems, which encompass hospitals, physician groups, and outpatient facilities, the offering brings inventory and medical support activities together in a consolidated service center and connects the center to points of care through dedicated transportation and final-mile delivery.\n\nDHL Supply Chain Expands Service Logistics Capabilities to Accelerate Data Center Infrastructure Parts Delivery\n\nThe expanded data center logistics network speeds up delivery of mission-critical installation and replacement parts to key facilities in hours rather than days.\n\nDHL Awards Ultimate Small Business INDYCAR Sweepstakes Prize to FLATED Following Nationwide Promotion for U.S. SME’s\n\nFLATED’s logo will be prominently displayed on the No. 10 DHL Chip Ganassi Racing Honda driven by four-time INDYCAR champion and 2025 Indianapolis 500 winner Alex Palou, and its leadership will receive a VIP race weekend experience, courtesy of DHL.\n\nU.S. Shoppers: Speed, Trust, and Transparency Now Decide Online Purchase\n\nThe report, based on responses from 1,000 U.S. shoppers across generations, reveals a market where expectations for speed, trust, and seamless experiences continue to accelerate.\n\nGeneral Motors Names DHL Supply Chain North America a 2025 Supplier of the Year\n\nThe award recognizes suppliers that demonstrate exceptional performance across key categories including safety, execution, resilience and customer support, as evaluated by a global GM team.\n\nDHL Highlights North America’s Trade Resilience Ahead of USMCA Review, Sees Opportunities and Competitiveness from Trade Agreements\n\nThis comes as policymakers from the United States, Mexico, and Canada prepare for the 2026 Joint Review of the United States-Mexico-Canada Agreement (USMCA).\n\nDHL Partners With Stasher to Offer Convenient Luggage Storage and Shipping Solutions for Travelers\n\nThrough this partnership, travelers can securely store luggage at participating DHL ServicePoint and DHL Premier Partner locations across the U.S.\n\nDHL eCommerce and USPS Enter $10 Billion - Plus, Long‑term Exclusive Agreement\n\nAt an expected value well over $10 billion (USD), the agreement is unprecedented in the 25-year DHL eCommerce-USPS relationship and positions both organizations for long-term competitive success.\n\nDHL Supply Chain Announces Leadership Appointments to Advance Strategy 2x30\n\nJim Monkmeyer, currently President, Transportation, DHL Supply Chain North America, has been appointed Global Head of LLP & Supply Chain Orchestration, DHL Supply Chain, effective immediately.\n\nDiscover all the latest global news from DHL by taking a look at our recent global press releases\n\nThis resource center for journalists housing our latest global press releases, useful multimedia materials, a list of press events and a direct link to our spokespersons.\n\nAccess useful images, tv footage, videos, infographics, facts and figures.\n\nFind the right contacts for media inquiries and information.\n\nLatest news and extensive press material for the DHL Group.\n\nGet to know the world's leading postal and logistics group, DHL Group\n\nThese technologies are used to ensure that our website operates correctly and they cannot be deactivated.\n\nThese technologies collect information about the way our website is used, such as the Internet browser and operating system used, domain name of the website from which you accessed our site, number of visits, average time spent on the site and pages viewed.\n\nThese technologies allow the website to remember choices you make and provide enhanced, more personal features. For example, these technologies can be used to remember and store the last tracking number that you entered when using a tracking application. Information these technologies collect may be anonymized and they cannot track your browsing activity on other websites.\n\nWe use analytics technologies to improve the quality of our website and its content, and to ensure that our partners’ embedded services work properly.\n\nYouTube technologies are used when users call up web pages that play embedded YouTube videos. Youtube.com is a Google-owned video hosting and sharing platform. Youtube.com collects user data through embedded videos, which is aggregated with data from other Google services in order to display targeted advertising to website visitors.\n\nThese technologies may be set through our site by our advertising partners. They may be used by those companies to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant adverts on other sites. They do not store directly personal information, but are based on uniquely identifying your browser and internet device. If you do not allow these technologies, you will experience less targeted advertising.\n\nWe use Google technologies to ensure that the Google mapping data used in the location finder is displayed correctly and completely. These technologies may incorporate data transfers in countries without an adequate level of data protection. The map in the location finder cannot be displayed unless you accept these technologies.\n\nWe use Bing technologies to ensure that the Bing mapping data used in the location finder is displayed correctly and completely. The map in the location finder cannot be displayed unless you accept these technologies."
